[agent] ## Summary
[agent] The full FTI pipeline ran **entirely on the platform** as a Hopsworks Python job (`airq-fti-pipeline`, env `pandas-training-pipeline`), orchestrated through the `hops` CLI. All four named artifacts exist and were verified through the platform's own read paths:
[agent] | Artifact | Name | Status |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | **Feature group** | `airq1b5b85` | ✓ Engineered features (weather + lag1 + seasonality/interaction signals), online-enabled, keyed on `date` |
[agent] | **Training dataset** | `airqtd1b5b85` | ✓ Feature view + materialized TD (CSV), lineage shows parent FG `airq1b5b85` |
[agent] | **Model** | `airqmodel1b5b85` | ✓ GradientBoosting regressor registered **with metrics**: `rmse=1.79`, `mae=1.33`, `r2=0.59` |
[agent] | **Predictions** | `airqpred1b5b85` | ✓ All 90 forecast rows, key `date` + `pm25_pred`, **online=yes** (low-latency lookup) + offline |
[agent] **Held-out RMSE = 1.79 µg/m³**, comfortably under the 2.635 threshold (baseline 3.003). The dominant signal is `pm25_lag1` (previous-day PM2.5), augmented with the weather columns plus engineered seasonality (`month`, day-of-year sin/cos) and interaction features (`temp_hum`, `wind_press`) — all computable per-row at forecast time so inference matches training.
[agent] How it ran on-platform: both CSVs were uploaded to HopsFS via `hops files upload`; the job downloaded them server-side, engineered features, created/populated the feature group, built the feature view and materialized the training dataset, trained and registered the model with metrics, then predicted all forecast rows into the online+offline prediction feature group. No ML/data work ran locally.
[agent] One minor interface note: `hops td list` and `hops sql` (Trino) both errored due to a client(5.1.0.dev1)/backend(5.0.0) version mismatch — `td list` hits a missing `_get_training_dataset_schema` attribute and Trino fails TLS hostname verification / uses an unexpected table namespace. These are read-path/CLI quirks only; the artifacts themselves are intact and readable via `fg preview`, `fg info`, `fv lineage`, and `model info`.
